{
  "id": "ep250",
  "duration": 54.441,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 17.1,
      "text": "A single tunnel on the Moon is wide enough to hold Philadelphia.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Earthshine bigger.webp",
        "credit": "Keck Institute for Space Studies",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earthshine_bigger.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 8.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.533,
          "end": 17.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.1,
      "end": 20.82,
      "text": "Most people see the Moon as a solid, cratered rock baked by radiation.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Part of the Moon's surface, Artemis 1.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Part_of_the_Moon%27s_surface,_Artemis_1.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.1,
          "end": 20.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 20.82,
      "end": 26.48,
      "text": "But in 2009, the Japanese Kaguya spacecraft spotted a massive dark pit in the Marius Hills.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Marius Hills Pit - Lava Tube Skylight? (LROC202 - KaguyaTerrainCamera 039).png",
        "credit": "NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marius_Hills_Pit_-_Lava_Tube_Skylight%3F_(LROC202_-_KaguyaTerrainCamera_039).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 20.833,
          "end": 26.467,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 26.48,
      "end": 30.12,
      "text": "This skylight is actually a collapsed roof over an ancient lava tube.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Diversity of Basaltic Lunar Volcanism (LROC702 - MHpit crop).png",
        "credit": "NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Diversity_of_Basaltic_Lunar_Volcanism_(LROC702_-_MHpit_crop).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 26.467,
          "end": 30.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 30.12,
      "end": 34.66,
      "text": "These tunnels formed billions of years ago when molten rivers cooled and drained away.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Art Institute of Chicago (CC0)",
        "title": "The Eruption of Vesuvius",
        "credit": "Pierre-Jacques Volaire (French, 1729\u20131799)",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://www.artic.edu/artworks/57996"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 30.133,
          "end": 34.667,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.66,
      "end": 39.9,
      "text": "On Earth, lava tubes are cramped, but the Moon's low gravity allows them to reach impossible sizes.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Rangitoto Island lava cave 2.jpg",
        "credit": "Mx. Granger",
        "license": "CC0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rangitoto_Island_lava_cave_2.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.667,
          "end": 37.133,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 37.133,
          "end": 39.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 39.9,
      "end": 44.36,
      "text": "Theoretical models show these rock cathedrals can stay stable at widths of five kilometers.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Inside a Lava Tube (ae4b0a7b-7121-4f23-9c86-f9ef4141c375).jpg",
        "credit": "NPS Photo",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Inside_a_Lava_Tube_(ae4b0a7b-7121-4f23-9c86-f9ef4141c375).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 42.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 42.133,
          "end": 44.367,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 44.36,
      "end": 49.58,
      "text": "In 2024, radar confirmed an accessible cave conduit beneath the Sea of Tranquility.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "1-s2.0-S0012821X24003510-gr10 lrg.jpg",
        "credit": "Marcin Chwa\u0142a, Goro Komatsu, Junichi Haruyama",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1-s2.0-S0012821X24003510-gr10_lrg.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 44.367,
          "end": 46.567,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 46.567,
          "end": 49.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 49.58,
      "end": 54.091,
      "text": "Future colonists will find safety inside a tunnel on the Moon wide enough to hold Philadelphia.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Earthshine bigger.webp",
        "credit": "Keck Institute for Space Studies",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earthshine_bigger.webp"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 49.567,
          "end": 54.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
